\details{
The stlnpp package provides a framework for handling,
visualising, and analysing spatio-temporal point patterns constrained
to linear networks. It implements methods for estimating intensity functions
using kernel and Voronoi-based approaches, enabling the study of spatial heterogeneity.
The package also facilitates the assessment of spatial interactions between points
through second- and higher-order summary statistics, allowing for a detailed
characterisation of point pattern structure beyond first-order effects.
